text:
julia-cs: Hey team — Acme (acct acme-prod) reporting ~12 card declines in last hour. All declines show 3DS failure: ACS returned \"session_expired\" right after our tokenization step. Customer says card was tokenized then charged immediately.

alex-payments: Do we have an example trace_id + event id? Are these only tokenized cards or raw PAN too?

julia-cs: Only tokenized so far (they use our hosted tokenization widget). Sample event: evt_01H8XK2Z9A0, trace: tr_20260317_01. Happened on region eu-west-1.

samir-eng: Thanks — prelim checks: no widespread ACS outages in dashboards. Can you paste the raw gateway response payload? Also tag payments-bot to look for recent rule changes.

julia-cs: Pasted minimal sanitized payload below:
```json
{ "event_id": "evt_01H8XK2Z9A0", "merchant": "acme-prod", "method": "token_charge", "status": "decline", "decline_code": "3ds_session_expired", "acs_url": "https://acs.bank.example/3ds", "timestamp": "2026-03-17T16:42:10Z" }
```

payments-bot: Automated alert: spike_detected=card_declines 2026-03-17T16:40:00Z -> 16:50:00Z (+340% vs baseline). Top merchant: acme-prod. Correlation: recent cookies config change on proxy layer.

marta-sre: FYI I rolled a change yesterday that tightened SameSite defaults for cookies to Strict in the auth proxy (attempt to harden CSRF surface). Could be breaking cross-site 3DS iframe flows. Rolling back to previous SameSite=None for payment flows is an option.

alex-payments: That would explain ACS dropping the 3DS session — the ACS iframe needs the cardholder session cookie to be available. If SameSite=Strict/Default then cross-site iframe won't send cookie -> ACS thinks session timed out.

samir-eng: Can we reproduce locally? 3DS requires a real iframe interaction. I prepared a puppeteer repro to simulate tokenization + redirect to ACS iframe. Julia, can you run this in a staging tenant with acme's settings?

samir-eng: ```js
// puppeteer snippet to repro 3DS iframe cookie behavior
const puppeteer = require('puppeteer');
(async () => {
  const b = await puppeteer.launch({headless: true});
  const p = await b.newPage();
  await p.goto('https://staging-hosted-tokenizer.example/acme-prod');
  // trigger tokenization then open checkout which embeds ACS iframe
  await p.click('#tokenize-and-pay');
  await p.waitForSelector('iframe#acs');
  const frame = await p.frames().find(f => f.name() === 'acs');
  console.log('acs cookie present:', await frame.evaluate(() => document.cookie));
  await b.close();
})();
```

julia-cs: Running now on staging -> will post results.

(3 minutes later)

julia-cs: Repro on staging: frame document.cookie is empty when SameSite=Strict set. When I flip proxy cookie to SameSite=None it populates and 3DS completes.

alex-payments: Ok root cause confirmed: proxy change -> SameSite cookie tightened -> ACS iframe loses session -> issuer responds session_expired -> declines.

marta-sre: Rolling back auth proxy cookie SameSite change for payment routes now. ETA 10m. I'll also add an allowlist for payment-related domains so we don't accidentally tighten again.

ops-bot: Deploy rollback started: deploy_id=rb_20260317_12, started_by=marta-sre.

(8 minutes later)

marta-sre: Rollback complete. Monitoring.

payments-bot: Post-rollback check: decline spike reduced to +8% vs baseline over last 10m. Top affected merchant still acme-prod but failed count down from 12 -> 1.

samir-eng: Nice. Next steps:
- Temporarily keep SameSite=None for cookies used by hosted tokenization / checkout flows.
- Add regression test in CDN/proxy that simulates cross-site iframe cookie presence.
- Add alert rule to detect cookie-policy deploys that modify SameSite for routes tagged payment.*
- Notify product/security of exception with timeline.

julia-cs: I've informed Acme (low-friction incident): explained cause and ETA, will follow up when all clear.

alex-payments: I'll add a KB note for support about recognizing 3DS \"session_expired\" pattern when cookie policies changed, include the puppeteer repro snippet.

marta-sre: I'll file a postmortem draft and link the rollback runbook.

julia-cs: Thanks all :heart: — closing thread when we confirm zero residual declines in next 30m.
